; Each boundary's exact seconds, then ONE ULP BELOW it. The pair is the
; gate: at the boundary the answer is the segment's own start tick, and
; one ulp below it is the tick before — because a clock value floors, "a
; clock value is the last tick BEGUN" (plan 03; `TimeMap`'s own header).
; A host that rounded instead of flooring, or that lost the last bit
; anywhere in the conversion, moves one of these six lines.
(times "3FDEB851EB851EB8" "3FDEB851EB851EB7")
(times "3FEC28F5C28F5C29" "3FEC28F5C28F5C28")
(times "3FF2E147AE147AE1" "3FF2E147AE147AE0")
